[list]
[*]Stands now dress for recreation as well as work. Tick Recreation on a stand and whoever comes to that room to enjoy themselves changes on the way in and back on the way out — a robe for the sauna, black tie for the games room. A room the game scores as a rec room turns it on by itself; a throne room, a dining room or a pool does not, and takes the switch by hand. Recreation and work types are mutually exclusive on a stand, because one outfit serves one purpose.
[*]Drinking, drug-taking and reading are not caught, and a recreation stand in open ground is refused for now — every outdoor cell belongs to one enormous room, so it would dress colonists for every walk on the map. Serving open ground needs a boundary of its own, and that is planned.
[*]Set owners now takes a list rather than a single colonist, with All / Men / Women filter tabs and an Assign all button. This matters most for gendered clothing: a stand serves anyone who can wear something on it, so a shared stand holding a prestige robe, a ladies hat and a formal shirt will put a man in the robe and leave the hat. Two clicks make it the women's stand, whether the colony has four colonists or forty.
[*]Change the whole outfit, off by default, is the difference between a lab coat worn over ordinary clothes and a sauna robe worn instead of them. Ticked, the colonist undresses completely and wears only what the stand holds — losing whatever their own clothes were providing, warmth included, which is worth a thought before putting a robe rack in a cold biome.
[/list]
